(4) a staged sieve (funnel): continuing one kept member from depth B1 to B2 by itself costs one reduction of N mod s for each
    prime s in (B1, B2]. That is tau = (reduction)/(Fermat test) of a test each, with tau ~ 1e-4 at 664 bits by word counts:
    about 11 word divisions for a reduction against about 664*(2*11^2) multiply-adds for a test. Testing the member at B1
    instead costs 1/p'(B1) tests. Continuation is worth it only if pi(B2) - pi(B1) < (1/p'(B1))/tau primes:
   B1 = 1e+06: 1/p' = 18.6; with tau = 0.001, continuing beats testing only over fewer than 18,562 primes, i.e. to B2 = B1 + about 256,438 (c changes by 1.625%)
   B1 = 1e+06: 1/p' = 18.6; with tau = 0.0001, continuing beats testing only over fewer than 185,616 primes, i.e. to B2 = B1 + about 2,564,382 (c changes by 8.425%)
   B1 = 1e+07: 1/p' = 15.9; with tau = 0.001, continuing beats testing only over fewer than 15,910 primes, i.e. to B2 = B1 + about 256,438 (c changes by 0.157%)
   B1 = 1e+07: 1/p' = 15.9; with tau = 0.0001, continuing beats testing only over fewer than 159,100 primes, i.e. to B2 = B1 + about 2,564,382 (c changes by 1.397%)
